course: dictionary
lesson: 15873
title: Unhygienic: dirty and risky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unhygienic means dirty in a way that can spread germs and illness. The prefix un- means not, so unhygienic is the opposite of hygienic, which means clean and safe.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The café was closed after inspectors found unhygienic kitchens.» Inspectors close a café only when it is a risk to health, so the kitchens must have been able to make people ill.
explain: Dirt and unhygienic are not always the same. A muddy football boot is dirty, but a kitchen where food touches germs is unhygienic, because germs can spread and make people ill.
fact: Hygienic means clean in a way that keeps germs away.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unhygienic means not hygienic.
fact: Germs are tiny living things that can make you ill.
fact: Unhygienic habits include not washing your hands before eating and coughing without covering your mouth.
fact: Unhygienic kitchens in cafés can make people ill, which is why inspectors check them.
exercise: «The café was closed after inspectors found unhygienic kitchens.» What does unhygienic mean? | Full of happy customers | Cold and wet | Very large and bright | *Dirty in a way that can spread germs
exercise: «Ravi coughed into his hand, then touched the shared cups. That was unhygienic.» Why was it unhygienic? | He was late for lunch | He was too quiet | The cups were too heavy | *Germs from his hand could spread to the cups
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unhygienic? | Careless | Sticky | Noisy | *Clean and safe
test: A sign in the kitchen says, «Unhygienic food may make you ill.» What does unhygienic suggest? | *Food that may carry germs and cause illness | Food that is clean and safe | Food that is free for everyone | Food that tastes sweet
test: «Do not share cups when you have a cold, it is unhygienic.» What is the main risk? | Your cold will go away | The cups will be too heavy | *Germs could spread to other people | The cups will break
exam: Jayden says, «A messy bedroom is always unhygienic.» Is he right? | No, because bedrooms cannot have germs | Yes, because messy rooms are always noisy | *No, it is only unhygienic if germs can spread and make people ill | Yes, any mess is unhygienic
